      "practice_mapping_verdict": "PASS",
      "summary": "Verified against the current 247 CMR 9.00 PDF (9.01(3), (4), (15), (16); 9.16(7)-(8); 9.19(1)(g), (j), (23), (24); 9.20), 247 CMR 2.00 (licensee undefined there too), 247 CMR 14.01, 247 CMR 6.02(5)-(6) and 6.09, Board Policy 2023-07 (rev. 2/6/25), M.G.L. c. 94C, s. 21 (label and telephone provisions confirmed as separate fourth and fifth paragraphs, so the s. 39I inpatient exception reaches only the telephone paragraph), and M.G.L. c. 112, ss. 39D, 39F-39J. The substantive teaching is accurate: the two cumulative limbs of 9.01(4); 9.01(3)'s most-current/each-chapter duty and its 'unless otherwise regulated by the Board' qualifier, correctly distinguished from the statutory USP (all chapters) duty in ss. 39G(a)(4), 39H(a)(4), 39I(a)(5) with the (c)(4) no-exemption proviso and the s. 39D USP definition including the National Formulary; 9.01(15)'s three descriptors and two exceptions, with the section's interpretive readings (extenuating circumstances, referral) clearly labelled as readings; Policy 2023-07 presented as guidance with accurate quotations (reconstitution, flavoring, complex examples, not all inclusive); 9.01(16)'s two duties with a properly hedged safe course on disclosures; the s. 21 label reaching every Board-licensed compounding pharmacy, the telephone line's two conditions, 56-hour/every-day staffing, pharmacist-with-records requirement, placement, and the narrow institutional inpatient exception; and a hedged, correctly sourced safe course for non-resident compounding pharmacies under 247 CMR 6.02 and 9.20. Three Low findings: a table cell says the Board 'grants' a waiver if it finds the conditions (14.01 says 'may'); the 9.16(7) profile duty is stated without the 9.16(8) institutional sterile compounding pharmacy exception; and a trap says the 9.19(1)(g)/(j) requirements are subject 'only' to 9.19(23)/(24), ignoring a 14.01 waiver. All eight practice questions (MA-Q-0117, 0314, 0316, 0321, 0327, 0399, 0421, 0422) are answerable from and consistent with the section. MINOR_EDIT for the three wording corrections; no Medium or higher defect."
